{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "c3a7f1e2-5b64-4a19-9d3c-central-identity",
    "name": "Central Identity — Seffro & Helppu",
    "description": "# Central Identity API\n\nOne shared account across every application, with no shared login site.\n\n## Getting started\n\n1. Set `identity_url` and `service_secret` in the collection variables. Get a secret with `npm run create-client <name>` on the identity service.\n2. Run **Register**, then **Login**. Login stores `access_token` and `refresh_token` automatically, so the authenticated requests work without copying anything.\n\n## Two surfaces\n\n- **Folder 1** is the identity service itself: private, server-to-server, guarded by `X-Service-Secret`. In production this is not reachable from the internet.\n- **Folders 2 and 3** are the Laravel apps' own mobile APIs. They call folder 1 internally and additionally manage the local user record.\n\n## Things worth knowing\n\n- `register` never returns a token. Registration and authentication are separate steps, which is what makes email verification enforceable.\n- A duplicate email returns `user_exists: true` and nothing else — no central id.\n- `validate-token` is the only inspection endpoint; there is deliberately no signature-only check.\n- Logout blacklists the access token too, if you send the Authorization header.\n\nSee HOW-IT-WORKS.md for the full walkthrough.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Identity Service (internal)",
      "description": "Server-to-server API. Every request needs X-Service-Secret; these are called by your Laravel backends, never by a browser. Set identity_url and service_secret first.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identity_url}}/api/health",
              "host": [
                "{{identity_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The only unauthenticated route. Use it for load-balancer probes; it does not touch the database."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"ok\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Service-Secret",
                "value": "{{service_secret}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identity_url}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": [
                "{{identity_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates the identity and returns NO session — registration and authentication are separate steps.\n\n201 { central_user_id, verification_required }\n200 { user_exists: true }  — address already registered; no central id is returned, because nothing here proves the caller owns that address.\n\nSend the user to Login next.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"CorrectHorse123\",\n  \"first_name\": \"John\",\n  \"last_name\": \"Doe\",\n  \"phone\": \"5551234567\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.central_user_id) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('central_user_id', body.central_user_id);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"no session issued\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property(\"access_token\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Service-Secret",
                "value": "{{service_secret}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identity_url}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{identity_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The only path that issues a session, and the only place email verification is enforced.\n\n200 { access_token, refresh_token, expires_in, token_type, user }\n401 wrong password, or account suspended/banned\n403 EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED  — when REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION is on\n423 ACCOUNT_LOCKED      — too many failed attempts\n\nSaves access_token and refresh_token to collection variables.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"john@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"CorrectHorse123\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.access_token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', body.refresh_token);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"returns a session\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"access_token\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Service-Secret",
                "value": "{{service_secret}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identity_url}}/api/auth/validate-token",
              "host": [
                "{{identity_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "validate-token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The only token-inspection endpoint. Checks the signature and everything a signature cannot know: revocation, account status, verification.\n\n200 { valid: true, user }\n401 { valid: false, reason } where reason is invalid_token | token_revoked | account_inactive | email_unverified\n\nApplications verify locally with the public key on hot paths and call this periodically (CENTRAL_AUTH_REVALIDATE_EVERY) or before privileged actions."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"valid\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().valid).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Service-Secret",
                "value": "{{service_secret}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identity_url}}/api/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{identity_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Rotates the pair: the presented refresh token is spent and a new one issued. Replaying a spent token fails — which is also how token theft surfaces.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"{{refresh_token}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.access_token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', body.access_token);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refresh_token', body.refresh_token);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test(\"returns a session\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"access_token\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
